---CreateNFSFileShareInput
---@class aws.storage_gateway.CreateNFSFileShareInput
---@field ClientToken aws.storage_gateway.ClientToken A unique string value that you supply that is used by S3 File Gateway to ensure idempotent file share creation.
---@field NFSFileShareDefaults? aws.storage_gateway.NFSFileShareDefaults File share default values. Optional.
---@field GatewayARN aws.storage_gateway.GatewayARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the S3 File Gateway on which you want to create a file share.
---@field EncryptionType? aws.storage_gateway.EncryptionType|string A value that specifies the type of server-side encryption that the file share will use for the data that it stores in Amazon S3.
---@field KMSEncrypted? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean Optional. Set to true to use Amazon S3 server-side encryption with your own KMS key (SSE-KMS), or false to use a key managed by Amazon S3 (SSE-S3). To use dual-layer encryption (DSSE-KMS), set the EncryptionType parameter instead.
---@field KMSKey? aws.storage_gateway.KMSKey Optional. The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a symmetric customer master key (CMK) used for Amazon S3 server-side encryption. Storage Gateway does not support asymmetric CMKs. This value must be set if KMSEncrypted is true, or if EncryptionType is SseKms or DsseKms.
---@field Role aws.storage_gateway.Role The ARN of the Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that an S3 File Gateway assumes when it accesses the underlying storage.
---@field LocationARN aws.storage_gateway.LocationARN A custom ARN for the backend storage used for storing data for file shares. It includes a resource ARN with an optional prefix concatenation. The prefix must end with a forward slash (/).
---@field DefaultStorageClass? aws.storage_gateway.StorageClass The default storage class for objects put into an Amazon S3 bucket by the S3 File Gateway. The default value is S3_STANDARD. Optional.
---@field ObjectACL? aws.storage_gateway.ObjectACL|string A value that sets the access control list (ACL) permission for objects in the S3 bucket that a S3 File Gateway puts objects into. The default value is private.
---@field ClientList? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareClientList The list of clients that are allowed to access the S3 File Gateway. The list must contain either valid IPv4/IPv6 addresses or valid CIDR blocks.
---@field Squash? aws.storage_gateway.Squash A value that maps a user to anonymous user.
---@field ReadOnly? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets the write status of a file share. Set this value to true to set the write status to read-only, otherwise set to false.
---@field GuessMIMETypeEnabled? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that enables guessing of the MIME type for uploaded objects based on file extensions. Set this value to true to enable MIME type guessing, otherwise set to false. The default value is true.
---@field RequesterPays? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets who pays the cost of the request and the cost associated with data download from the S3 bucket. If this value is set to true, the requester pays the costs; otherwise, the S3 bucket owner pays. However, the S3 bucket owner always pays the cost of storing data.
---@field Tags? aws.storage_gateway.Tags A list of up to 50 tags that can be assigned to the NFS file share. Each tag is a key-value pair.
---@field FileShareName? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareName The name of the file share. Optional.
---@field CacheAttributes? aws.storage_gateway.CacheAttributes Specifies refresh cache information for the file share.
---@field NotificationPolicy? aws.storage_gateway.NotificationPolicy The notification policy of the file share. SettlingTimeInSeconds controls the number of seconds to wait after the last point in time a client wrote to a file before generating an ObjectUploaded notification. Because clients can make many small writes to files, it's best to set this parameter for as long as possible to avoid generating multiple notifications for the same file in a small time period...
---@field VPCEndpointDNSName? aws.storage_gateway.DNSHostName Specifies the DNS name for the VPC endpoint that the NFS file share uses to connect to Amazon S3.
---@field BucketRegion? aws.storage_gateway.RegionId Specifies the Region of the S3 bucket where the NFS file share stores files.
---@field AuditDestinationARN? aws.storage_gateway.AuditDestinationARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the storage used for audit logs.

---CreateNFSFileShareOutput
---@class aws.storage_gateway.CreateNFSFileShareOutput
---@field FileShareARN? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the newly created file share.

---CreateSMBFileShareInput
---@class aws.storage_gateway.CreateSMBFileShareInput
---@field ClientToken aws.storage_gateway.ClientToken A unique string value that you supply that is used by S3 File Gateway to ensure idempotent file share creation.
---@field GatewayARN aws.storage_gateway.GatewayARN The ARN of the S3 File Gateway on which you want to create a file share.
---@field EncryptionType? aws.storage_gateway.EncryptionType|string A value that specifies the type of server-side encryption that the file share will use for the data that it stores in Amazon S3.
---@field KMSEncrypted? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean Optional. Set to true to use Amazon S3 server-side encryption with your own KMS key (SSE-KMS), or false to use a key managed by Amazon S3 (SSE-S3). To use dual-layer encryption (DSSE-KMS), set the EncryptionType parameter instead.
---@field KMSKey? aws.storage_gateway.KMSKey Optional. The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a symmetric customer master key (CMK) used for Amazon S3 server-side encryption. Storage Gateway does not support asymmetric CMKs. This value must be set if KMSEncrypted is true, or if EncryptionType is SseKms or DsseKms.
---@field Role aws.storage_gateway.Role The ARN of the Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that an S3 File Gateway assumes when it accesses the underlying storage.
---@field LocationARN aws.storage_gateway.LocationARN A custom ARN for the backend storage used for storing data for file shares. It includes a resource ARN with an optional prefix concatenation. The prefix must end with a forward slash (/).
---@field DefaultStorageClass? aws.storage_gateway.StorageClass The default storage class for objects put into an Amazon S3 bucket by the S3 File Gateway. The default value is S3_STANDARD. Optional.
---@field ObjectACL? aws.storage_gateway.ObjectACL|string A value that sets the access control list (ACL) permission for objects in the S3 bucket that a S3 File Gateway puts objects into. The default value is private.
---@field ReadOnly? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets the write status of a file share. Set this value to true to set the write status to read-only, otherwise set to false.
---@field GuessMIMETypeEnabled? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that enables guessing of the MIME type for uploaded objects based on file extensions. Set this value to true to enable MIME type guessing, otherwise set to false. The default value is true.
---@field RequesterPays? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets who pays the cost of the request and the cost associated with data download from the S3 bucket. If this value is set to true, the requester pays the costs; otherwise, the S3 bucket owner pays. However, the S3 bucket owner always pays the cost of storing data.
---@field SMBACLEnabled? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean Set this value to true to enable access control list (ACL) on the SMB file share. Set it to false to map file and directory permissions to the POSIX permissions.
---@field AccessBasedEnumeration? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean The files and folders on this share will only be visible to users with read access.
---@field AdminUserList? aws.storage_gateway.UserList A list of users or groups in the Active Directory that will be granted administrator privileges on the file share. These users can do all file operations as the super-user. Acceptable formats include: DOMAIN\User1, user1, @group1, and @DOMAIN\group1.
---@field ValidUserList? aws.storage_gateway.UserList A list of users or groups in the Active Directory that are allowed to access the file share. A group must be prefixed with the @ character. Acceptable formats include: DOMAIN\User1, user1, @group1, and @DOMAIN\group1. Can only be set if Authentication is set to ActiveDirectory.
---@field InvalidUserList? aws.storage_gateway.UserList A list of users or groups in the Active Directory that are not allowed to access the file share. A group must be prefixed with the @ character. Acceptable formats include: DOMAIN\User1, user1, @group1, and @DOMAIN\group1. Can only be set if Authentication is set to ActiveDirectory.
---@field AuditDestinationARN? aws.storage_gateway.AuditDestinationARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the storage used for audit logs.
---@field Authentication? aws.storage_gateway.Authentication The authentication method that users use to access the file share. The default is ActiveDirectory.
---@field CaseSensitivity? aws.storage_gateway.CaseSensitivity|string The case of an object name in an Amazon S3 bucket. For ClientSpecified, the client determines the case sensitivity. For CaseSensitive, the gateway determines the case sensitivity. The default value is ClientSpecified.
---@field Tags? aws.storage_gateway.Tags A list of up to 50 tags that can be assigned to the NFS file share. Each tag is a key-value pair.
---@field FileShareName? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareName The name of the file share. Optional.
---@field CacheAttributes? aws.storage_gateway.CacheAttributes Specifies refresh cache information for the file share.
---@field NotificationPolicy? aws.storage_gateway.NotificationPolicy The notification policy of the file share. SettlingTimeInSeconds controls the number of seconds to wait after the last point in time a client wrote to a file before generating an ObjectUploaded notification. Because clients can make many small writes to files, it's best to set this parameter for as long as possible to avoid generating multiple notifications for the same file in a small time period...
---@field VPCEndpointDNSName? aws.storage_gateway.DNSHostName Specifies the DNS name for the VPC endpoint that the SMB file share uses to connect to Amazon S3.
---@field BucketRegion? aws.storage_gateway.RegionId Specifies the Region of the S3 bucket where the SMB file share stores files.
---@field OplocksEnabled? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean Specifies whether opportunistic locking is enabled for the SMB file share.

---CreateSMBFileShareOutput
---@class aws.storage_gateway.CreateSMBFileShareOutput
---@field FileShareARN? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the newly created file share.

