---Describes Network File System (NFS) file share default values. Files and folders stored as Amazon S3 objects in S3 buckets don't, by default, have Unix file permissions assigned to them. Upon discovery in an S3 bucket by Storage Gateway, the S3 objects that represent files and folders are assigned these default Unix permissions. This operation is only supported for S3 File Gateways.
---@class aws.storage_gateway.NFSFileShareDefaults
---@field FileMode? aws.storage_gateway.PermissionMode The Unix file mode in the form "nnnn". For example, 0666 represents the default file mode inside the file share. The default value is 0666.
---@field DirectoryMode? aws.storage_gateway.PermissionMode The Unix directory mode in the form "nnnn". For example, 0666 represents the default access mode for all directories inside the file share. The default value is 0777.
---@field GroupId? aws.storage_gateway.PermissionId The default group ID for the file share (unless the files have another group ID specified). The default value is nfsnobody.
---@field OwnerId? aws.storage_gateway.PermissionId The default owner ID for files in the file share (unless the files have another owner ID specified). The default value is nfsnobody.

---The Unix file permissions and ownership information assigned, by default, to native S3 objects when an S3 File Gateway discovers them in S3 buckets. This operation is only supported in S3 File Gateways.
---@class aws.storage_gateway.NFSFileShareInfo
---@field NFSFileShareDefaults? aws.storage_gateway.NFSFileShareDefaults
---@field FileShareARN? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareARN
---@field FileShareId? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareId
---@field FileShareStatus? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareStatus
---@field GatewayARN? aws.storage_gateway.GatewayARN
---@field EncryptionType? aws.storage_gateway.EncryptionType A value that specifies the type of server-side encryption that the file share will use for the data that it stores in Amazon S3.
---@field KMSEncrypted aws.storage_gateway.Boolean2 Optional. Set to true to use Amazon S3 server-side encryption with your own KMS key (SSE-KMS), or false to use a key managed by Amazon S3 (SSE-S3). To use dual-layer encryption (DSSE-KMS), set the EncryptionType parameter instead.
---@field KMSKey? aws.storage_gateway.KMSKey
---@field Path? aws.storage_gateway.Path
---@field Role? aws.storage_gateway.Role
---@field LocationARN? aws.storage_gateway.LocationARN
---@field DefaultStorageClass? aws.storage_gateway.StorageClass The default storage class for objects put into an Amazon S3 bucket by the S3 File Gateway. The default value is S3_STANDARD. Optional.
---@field ObjectACL? aws.storage_gateway.ObjectACL
---@field ClientList? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareClientList
---@field Squash? aws.storage_gateway.Squash
---@field ReadOnly? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets the write status of a file share. Set this value to true to set the write status to read-only, otherwise set to false.
---@field GuessMIMETypeEnabled? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that enables guessing of the MIME type for uploaded objects based on file extensions. Set this value to true to enable MIME type guessing, otherwise set to false. The default value is true.
---@field RequesterPays? aws.storage_gateway.Boolean A value that sets who pays the cost of the request and the cost associated with data download from the S3 bucket. If this value is set to true, the requester pays the costs; otherwise, the S3 bucket owner pays. However, the S3 bucket owner always pays the cost of storing data.
---@field Tags? aws.storage_gateway.Tags A list of up to 50 tags assigned to the NFS file share, sorted alphabetically by key name. Each tag is a key-value pair. For a gateway with more than 10 tags assigned, you can view all tags using the ListTagsForResource API operation.
---@field FileShareName? aws.storage_gateway.FileShareName The name of the file share. Optional.
---@field CacheAttributes? aws.storage_gateway.CacheAttributes Refresh cache information for the file share.
---@field NotificationPolicy? aws.storage_gateway.NotificationPolicy The notification policy of the file share. SettlingTimeInSeconds controls the number of seconds to wait after the last point in time a client wrote to a file before generating an ObjectUploaded notification. Because clients can make many small writes to files, it's best to set this parameter for as long as possible to avoid generating multiple notifications for the same file in a small time period...
---@field VPCEndpointDNSName? aws.storage_gateway.DNSHostName Specifies the DNS name for the VPC endpoint that the NFS file share uses to connect to Amazon S3.
---@field BucketRegion? aws.storage_gateway.RegionId Specifies the Region of the S3 bucket where the NFS file share stores files.
---@field AuditDestinationARN? aws.storage_gateway.AuditDestinationARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the storage used for audit logs.

