---Describes a virtual tape object.
---@class aws.storage_gateway.Tape
---@field TapeARN? aws.storage_gateway.TapeARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the virtual tape.
---@field TapeBarcode? aws.storage_gateway.TapeBarcode The barcode that identifies a specific virtual tape.
---@field TapeCreatedDate? aws.storage_gateway.Time The date the virtual tape was created.
---@field TapeSizeInBytes? aws.storage_gateway.TapeSize The size, in bytes, of the virtual tape capacity.
---@field TapeStatus? aws.storage_gateway.TapeStatus The current state of the virtual tape.
---@field VTLDevice? aws.storage_gateway.VTLDeviceARN The virtual tape library (VTL) device that the virtual tape is associated with.
---@field Progress? aws.storage_gateway.DoubleObject For archiving virtual tapes, indicates how much data remains to be uploaded before archiving is complete.
---@field TapeUsedInBytes? aws.storage_gateway.TapeUsage The size, in bytes, of data stored on the virtual tape.
---@field KMSKey? aws.storage_gateway.KMSKey
---@field PoolId? aws.storage_gateway.PoolId The ID of the pool that contains tapes that will be archived. The tapes in this pool are archived in the S3 storage class that is associated with the pool. When you use your backup application to eject the tape, the tape is archived directly into the storage class (S3 Glacier or S3 Glacier Deep Archive) that corresponds to the pool.
---@field Worm aws.storage_gateway.Boolean2 If the tape is archived as write-once-read-many (WORM), this value is true.
---@field RetentionStartDate? aws.storage_gateway.Time The date that the tape is first archived with tape retention lock enabled.
